From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mtbl23 <mtbl23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:16:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Leaf port: skip the natural mob spawn cost lookup for types
 without a cost

NaturalSpawner#createState walks every loaded entity once per tick and, for
each countable mob, asked the environment attribute system for the
NATURAL_MOB_SPAWNS value at its position just to read its spawn cost. That is
a full-resolution biome lookup (BiomeManager, a chunk lookup through the chunk
system) per entity and was about a third of createState in the 12 bot Blitz
profile. Only a handful of entity types (soul sand valley, basalt delta, warped
forest mobs) have a cost in any biome.

The attribute system now records, when it is built, the union of the entity
types that have a spawn cost in its constant base value and in every biome's
NATURAL_MOB_SPAWNS entry (overlay and override only ever produce a subset of
that union). For any other type the cost is always null, so the lookup is
skipped. If the layer setup is anything other than constant base plus the one
biome layer, the set is unknown and every lookup is done as before.

Behaviour: identical results. The same shortcut is used in SpawnState#canSpawn
and #afterSpawn.

Motivated by Leaf's mob spawning changes (async counting makes createState free
in its profile); this is an independent, vanilla-identical implementation.
Leaf: https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf

